--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2989f6b7554baf142b3f807ffa71cecf, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialEntriesContainer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tutorialEntries:
  - id: 0
    tutorialEntryText: As a conductor, your job is to ensure passenger comfort and
      check their tickets. Passengers with invalid tickets should leave the train.
  - id: 1
    tutorialEntryText: To proceed to the next day you have to talk to at least one
      passenger. Proceed only if you do so.
  - id: 2
    tutorialEntryText: It is your personal <b>Diary</b>. Any thoughts that come to
      your mind about the passengers you spoke with will be recorded here.
  - id: 3
    tutorialEntryText: Once you enter a dialogue with a passenger, you cannot leave
      until you validate or reject the ticket. You can reject the ticket at any time
      by clicking proper dialogue option. Accepting the ticket is only possible after
      a properly conducted dialogue.
